const posts=[{slug:"one-edit-six-posts",title:"One edit can start six different conversations",date:"2026-10-21",excerpt:"Keep the finished edit, then give each destination its own opening, copy and release time.",content:"# One edit can start six different conversations\n\nFinishing the video and preparing its release are two creative decisions. The same useful result can need a different introduction on each platform.\n\n## Start with the useful outcome\n\nWrite down who the video helps and what they should understand after watching. Show that result early. A short clip of the finished work can explain more than a long tour of editor controls.\n\n## Give each post a reason to exist\n\nIn Publisher, inspect each destination rather than treating the first caption as final everywhere. Explain the workflow on LinkedIn, give a community a concrete discussion on Reddit, and make the visual result readable in a vertical version. Use the format and audience options available to the connected account.\n\n## Separate the clocks\n\nEach destination can have its own scheduled date and time. Review the timezone, then check the queue after scheduling. A saved release is different from a confirmed published post.\n\n## Learn from the actual response\n\nAllow for provider reporting delays and compare metrics with the same meaning. There is no guaranteed reach; the release gives you evidence for the next edit.\n"},{slug:"keep-the-edit-editable",title:"Keep the result. Keep the timeline.",date:"2026-10-21",excerpt:"A finished movie is useful. The project that explains every decision is useful again tomorrow.",content:"# Keep the result. Keep the timeline.\n\nA movie shows what the edit looks and sounds like. The saved project keeps the footage choices, layers, sound cues and motion that made it happen.\n\n## Save the decisions\n\nUse the Studio timeline to inspect the actual layers and timing. Select a target in Motion before changing its values, and use the inspector to reach the controls for that tool.\n\n## Check the complete movie\n\nWatch the whole export with sound. The opening, transitions, readable type and ending need to work together. A successful render alone is not a creative review.\n\n## Keep an independent backup\n\nSave the editable project and download a project backup before clearing browser storage or changing devices. Local browser projects and published platform copies are separate.\n\n## Make the next version deliberate\n\nReturn to the same timeline when revising the pacing, words or sound. Keeping the edit editable makes it easier to understand what you changed and why.\n"},{slug:"welcome",title:"Welcome to AutoPromote",date:"2026-01-02",content:"# Welcome to AutoPromote\n\nWe're excited to share a publishing platform focused on connected uploads, scheduling, analytics, and practical workflow improvements. This blog will feature product updates, release notes, and honest guidance about what is live, what depends on your setup, and what is still evolving.\n"},{slug:"release-2026-01",title:"January 2026 Release",date:"2026-01-02",content:"# January 2026 Release\n\nThis release includes improved scheduling, clearer platform-status handling, and product messaging that better matches the platform's current capabilities.\n"}];/* harmony default export */ const blog_posts = (posts);
